  "checks": [
    "AMD10 preserves exactly the prescribed global/infinite/finite measures and constructs Haar stabilizer measures for every original tuple, including degenerate tuples; all six MeasG.IsTextNorm clauses match.",
    "AMD11 uses the exact standard-frame hypothesis, the source multiplication order N then H, and all eight MeasW entries; its three identities plus eight Haar clauses reproduce the eleven printed normalization clauses.",
    "AMD12 fixes one original bridge before all words. Actual eC/fC/zC and nonzero original T supply frame_std, and the three group ties plus two word-indexed ties are literal MeasTieCore/MeasTie. The other source blocks, including Wb, stay supplied.",
    "AMD13 absorbs one finite positive Haar scalar in the second product factor without changing the first; trivial groups are included.",
    "AMD14 retains both infinity measures, both global measures, and the entire local S-measure family simultaneously. The original contract imposes no further restricted-product normalization between local S and finite S.",
    "AMD15 uses the actual Nsub on every vector in U-perp. Polynomial exp/log and the central F-ideal flag yield compact representatives by left rational translations; the conjugation in AMD.30 keeps the remainder in the preceding normal subgroup. The rational subgroup is exactly ratOf.",
    "AMD16 constructs a Borel transversal from finitely many translated small neighborhoods, proves finite positive Haar mass, and proves equality with every source fundamental-domain choice. Positive rescaling preserves null sets, so the choice-based real covolume is literally one.",
    "AMD17 installs the new global unipotent measure via the prescribed-measure theorem, keeping every stated infinity/global-H/local-S entry unchanged. Orbital and normalized local fiber comparisons are explicitly remaining inputs."
  ],
